{"beat": 8, "name": "HOW MAIL ORDER SHIPPED BEFORE", "text": "Now, mail order existed long before the parcel post. In 1911, Montgomery Ward, the oldest of the big catalogue houses, said it shipped 82% of its orders by rail freight, and only 8% by mail. Freight had its own staircase. The Sears catalogue explained it to customers in capital letters: railroad companies usually charge no more for carrying 100 pounds than they do for 20 pounds. So, it told them, if you only have a small order, get a friend to buy at the same time. Ship together. Split the minimum.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "Now,", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.3}, {"word": "mail", "start": 0.3, "end": 0.74}, {"word": "order", "start": 0.74, "end": 1.14}, {"word": "existed", "start": 1.14, "end": 1.6}, {"word": "long", "start": 1.6, "end": 2.06}, {"word": "before", "start": 2.06, "end": 2.34}, {"word": "the", "start": 2.34, "end": 2.52}, {"word": "parcel", "start": 2.52, "end": 2.88}, {"word": "post.", "start": 2.88, "end": 3.4}, {"word": "In", "start": 3.92, "end": 4.14}, {"word": "1911,", "start": 4.14, "end": 5.22}, {"word": "Montgomery", "start": 5.78, "end": 6.22}, {"word": "Ward,", "start": 6.22, "end": 6.88}, {"word": "the", "start": 7.28, "end": 7.36}, {"word": "oldest", "start": 7.36, "end": 7.78}, {"word": "of", "start": 7.78, "end": 8.02}, {"word": "the", "start": 8.02, "end": 8.14}, {"word": "big", "start": 8.14, "end": 8.34}, {"word": "catalogue", "start": 8.34, "end": 8.7}, {"word": "houses,", "start": 8.7, "end": 9.4}, {"word": "said", "start": 9.88, "end": 10.1}, {"word": "it", "start": 10.1, "end": 10.22}, {"word": "shipped", "start": 10.22, "end": 10.52}, {"word": "82%", "start": 10.52, "end": 10.94}, {"word": "of", "start": 11.52, "end": 11.68}, {"word": "its", "start": 11.68, "end": 11.82}, {"word": "orders", "start": 11.82, "end": 12.18}, {"word": "by", "start": 12.18, "end": 12.5}, {"word": "rail", "start": 12.5, "end": 12.84}, {"word": "freight,", "start": 12.84, "end